VIOLATION under rule-authoring.md — seven authoring properties breached, set out below in
eight numbered items because items (1) and (2) are the two halves of MUST-1: the hedged modal,
and the case handed back. Every breach is a defect in the CONTENT of
furniture that is fully present, so a judge scoring on shape alone finds nothing: the file has
frontmatter, an Origin, a Trust-Posture Wiring block, two numbered clauses, three justification
lines, two worked blocks and two BLOCKED corpora, exactly as its sibling does.

(1) MUST-1 (prohibitions, not encouragements) + MUST NOT § hedging. Both clause HEADINGS
announce obligations — "The Intake MUST Be Closed Before The Acknowledgement Channel" and
"A Committed Side Effect MUST Be Acked Rather Than Redelivered" — under a section still titled
"MUST Rules", while both BODIES hedge: "should normally", "should ideally", "is often the more
pragmatic choice". The word BLOCKED appears nowhere in either clause body.

(2) MUST-1, second half — each clause HANDS BACK the exact case its heading forbids. Clause 1:
"closing the connection directly in the signal handler is a reasonable call and the author is
generally best placed to judge it" — which licenses precisely the SIGTERM connection close the
Origin incident describes. Clause 2: "nacking at the deadline is a defensible trade-off",
licensing the redelivery that charged thirty-one cards twice.

(3) MUST-3 (every MUST clause has DO / DO NOT examples). Both worked blocks are present and
both are inert: the two arms are the SAME LINE. In clause 1 both arms read
"step 1: basic_cancel(tag); prefetch = 0", separated only by a trailing comment. In clause 2
both arms read "capture(charge_id) -> committed = True;  on shutdown: ack(msg)". The prohibited
construction — closing the connection first, nacking a committed message — is never shown, so
neither contract is learnable from its block.

(4) MUST-2 (BLOCKED phrases verbatim). Both corpora are present and both are third-person
abstractions: "reliance on broker-side redelivery semantics as a correctness mechanism",
"optimism regarding expected handler duration", "idempotency assumptions applied without
verification", "deadline-driven default selection under uncertainty". No session emits those
words, so the corpus is unrecognisable at the moment of the excuse and traps nothing.

(5) MUST NOT § "Rationale paragraphs longer than 2 sentences" + MUST-4. Both clause
justifications overrun and name no mechanism. Clause 1's appeals to what is "widely
acknowledged" and to "accumulated operational experience"; clause 2's defers to "how the
particular handler happens to be written" and to "the deduplication behaviour of whichever
component happens to sit downstream at the time". Neither states what actually goes wrong —
that an undeliverable ack reads at the broker as a dead consumer, and that redelivery restarts
the handler at line one.

(6) hook-output-discipline.md MUST-2 inversion in the Wiring severity. The row declares
"`block` at the hook layer whenever a diff contains a line mentioning `nack` or
`connection.close`" — `block` on a purely lexical trigger, the direction MUST-2 forbids — and
demotes gate-review to `advisory`, inverting both halves. The trigger would also fire on every
legitimate nack and every correct ordered close.

(7) rule-authoring.md MUST NOT § "`**Detection mechanism:**` row filing `Phase 2 (deferred)`
against a property only observable lexically". The deferral promises "a detector that
determines whether the author weighed the drain-deadline trade-off appropriately" and whether a
nack "reflected a considered judgement about handler idempotency rather than convenience".
Both are judgments over authorial intent with no parsed or structural signal, so the row books
teeth that cannot arrive. Contrast the sibling pole, whose deferral keys on two AST facts over
one patch.

(8) MUST-6 (Origin). Origin carries the same dated incident and the same measured blast radius
as the sibling, then closes on retrospective sentiment — "agreed that a shared understanding of
graceful shutdown would be valuable for everyone going forward" — instead of on what the
incident implies about the rule's FORM — so a later maintainer learns that the team felt bad,
not why this rule had to fix an order rather than ask for a judgement.

Shared surface that is NOT a finding. The frontmatter, the entire MUST NOT section including
its one-sentence mechanism-naming justification, the Grace period / Cumulative posture impact /
Regression-within-grace / Receipt requirement / Violation scope Wiring fields, and the first
three sentences of Origin are byte-identical with the sibling pole. A judge naming any of them,
or objecting that the detector is deferred at all, or that the rule is fictional, or that
`priority: 10` is wrong, has scored furniture rather than content. The pair is
surface-equalized: identical ordered `## ` heading list (MUST Rules / MUST NOT / Trust Posture
Wiring / Origin), two numbered clauses each, three `**Why:**` lines each, two worked blocks
each, two BLOCKED corpora each, at a size ratio under 1.01 — so shape answers nothing.
